          "thread": "Hack-to-full-recovery arc",
          "why": "Readers tracked Euler's improbable resurrection — from $197M stolen to $693M in deposits two years later — as a live proof-of-concept that a DeFi protocol can survive a catastrophic exploit and rebuild credibility."
        },
        {
          "source": "https://github.com/euler-xyz/euler-vault-kit",
          "thread": "v2 modular vault architecture",
          "why": "The open-source Euler Vault Kit and live v2 launch attracted builders curious whether a post-hack ground-up redesign could deliver genuinely new DeFi primitives rather than a patched v1."
        },
        {
          "source": "https://securitize.io/primary-market/vaneck-vbill",
          "thread": "Institutional RWA collateral integration",
          "why": "BlackRock's sBUIDL and VanEck's VBILL landing on Euler as on-chain loan collateral signaled to readers that tokenized real-world assets were finding a credible DeFi lending home, not just a marketing headline."
        },
        {
          "source": "https://www.euler.finance/blog/euler-q1-2026",
          "thread": "TVL growth scoreboard",
          "why": "Successive milestones — $133M, $387M, $600M, $2.15B — gave readers a concrete scoreboard to judge whether the post-hack comeback was durable or a temporary liquidity spike."
        },
        {
          "source": "",
          "thread": "CEO exit and institutional pivot",
          "why": "Michael Bentley stepping down and Euler pivoting explicitly toward institutional credit and RWAs raised questions about whether the protocol's community-DeFi identity was being traded for a TradFi-adjacent repositioning."
        }
      ]
