        {
          "dimension": "Smart-contract exploit recurrence",
          "level": "Medium",
          "note": "The original attack exploited a donation function in v1's collateral accounting; v2's EVC-based modular vault architecture redesigns this model, but the complexity of composable vaults and third-party curator integrations introduces fresh, less-audited attack surface.",
          "source": "https://www.chainalysis.com/blog/euler-finance-flash-loan-attack/"
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Curator concentration",
          "level": "Medium",
          "note": "v2 delegates risk management to external curators such as Concrete; if a small set of curators controls the majority of vault TVL, a single curator failure or misaligned incentive can cascade across the protocol without a direct Euler Labs circuit-breaker.",
          "source": "https://en.coin-turk.com/concrete-partners-with-euler-to-develop-institution-focused-defi-lending-solutions/"
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Regulatory",
          "level": "Medium",
          "note": "Euler's integration of permissioned zkVerified markets (Keyring/Avalanche) and SEC-registered tokenized treasury funds (sBUIDL, VBILL) as DeFi collateral increases regulatory surface area as securities regulators scrutinize tokenized-asset DeFi pipelines.",
          "source": "https://securitize.io/primary-market/vaneck-vbill"
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Liquidity migration",
          "level": "Medium",
          "note": "Fira's migration of $450M from Euler to its own fixed-rate protocol demonstrates that liquidity built on or beside Euler can exit rapidly when competing lending primitives offer structurally different terms, particularly for institutional borrowers requiring rate certainty.",
